{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths"]]},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DijkstraSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"DijkstraSearch.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ShortestPaths\/DijkstraSearch.swift#L17"},"modules":[{"name":"ShortestPaths"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DijkstraSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","role":"symbol","title":"DijkstraSearchEvent","externalID":"s:13ShortestPaths19DijkstraSearchEventO","symbolKind":"enum"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"What a Dijkstra search reports, in order, with the events of the Boost Graph Library’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Dijkstra visitor.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DijkstraSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edge","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Weight","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edge","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each source is discovered first, at distance zero. Then, while a discovered vertex is not yet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"settled, the one with the smallest distance is examined (settled at that distance), and each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of its out-edges is examined in turn with the distance it offers its target: the examined","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex’s distance plus the edge’s weight. An edge into an unsettled target is then relaxed,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when the offer is smaller than the target’s distance or the target was not yet discovered, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not relaxed. A relaxed edge to an undiscovered target is followed by that target’s discovery.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"An edge into a settled vertex, a self-loop included, is examined and nothing more. After its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"last out-edge the examined vertex is finished. Vertices the sources do not reach are never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/DijkstraSearchEvent\/discover(_:distance:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/DijkstraSearchEvent\/edgeNotRelaxed(_:distance:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/DijkstraSearchEvent\/edgeRelaxed(_:distance:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/DijkstraSearchEvent\/examine(_:distance:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/DijkstraSearchEvent\/examineEdge(_:distance:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/DijkstraSearchEvent\/finish(_:distance:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Enumeration Cases"},{"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/DijkstraSearchEvent\/Cus